NAME          HOLMES

*   Problem :
*   --------
*   Fit DNA data to a Baysian model to observe associations  between 
*   genetic variation and human disease risk. This is formulated as

*    min f(theta) =
*      - sum_{i=1}^m log[ 1 / ( 1 + e^{ - sum_{j=1}^n a_ij theta_j ) } ) ]
*      + 1/2 lambda sum_{j=1}^n theta_j^2
*    subject to theta geq 0

*   Problem defined and small-instance  simulated data provided by
*   Chris Holmes (Dept. Biostatistics, U. Oxford)
*   (cholmes@stats.ox.ac.uk)

*   SIF input: Nick Gould, April 2012
*   Updated to improve processing, Pim Heeman, May 2026.

*   classification OBR2-AN-180-0

*   Number of variables

 IE N                   180

*   Number of data points

 IE M                   1859

*   Regularization weight

*RE LAMBDA              0.001
 RE LAMBDA              0.0

*   other parameter definitions

 IE 1                   1

VARIABLES

 DO J         1                        N
 X  T(J)
 ND

GROUPS

 DO I         1                        N
 XN R(I)      T(I)      1.0
 ND

